# Tracer: generated Lean imports shared verifier rules through `Litex.Rules`.
#
# Before (the public module and namespace name were longer):
#   import Litex.BuiltinRules
#   exact Litex.BuiltinRules.notEqualSymmetry fact_a_ne_b
# Former behavior: generated proofs exposed the `BuiltinRules` name at every
# checked verifier-rule call site.
#
# Now (these facts exercise the renamed shared rule module):
forall a, b set:
    a != b
    =>:
        b != a

1 $in N
1 $in C
# Current To-Lean behavior: the generated file imports `Litex.Rules` and calls
# `Litex.Rules.notEqualSymmetry`, `Litex.Rules.numeralInN`, and
# `Litex.Rules.numeralInC`. It does not emit the former module name, repeat the
# semantic core, or repeat theorem bodies.
#
# Boundary: a verifier builtin without a checked shared-theorem adapter remains
# rejected by strict To-Lean; neither an inline tactic script nor an axiom is
# generated as a fallback.
# Evidence: `cargo test --release shared_builtin_rule_tracer_imports_theorems
# -- --nocapture` and `(cd lean && lake build)`.
